-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1116. hop-via.l4 with this file importing taken.l4 as well as
-- hop-b.l4, and naming `taken now` where it commits and `shop is closed` (which
-- is `taken now`) where it allows the buy: one rule reached by two import
-- paths. With every rule in one file the first trace gives two COMMITs and
-- WITHIN 10 and the second one COMMIT and WITHIN 9, and so must this.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT taken
IMPORT `hop-b`

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Bob
DECLARE Mode IS ONE OF peek, skip
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    go HAS mode IS A Mode
    buy

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`shop` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY buy PROVIDED NOT `shop is closed`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `taken` IS TRUE HENCE `shop`
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`start` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY go m
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `taken` IS (IF m EQUALS peek THEN NOT `taken now` ELSE TRUE) HENCE `shop`
    LEST FULFILLED

#TRACE `start` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Bob DOES go peek AT 1
    PARTY Bob DOES buy AT 2

#TRACE `start` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Bob DOES go skip AT 1
    PARTY Bob DOES buy AT 2
